Subject: [PATCH 20/20] Colour keys without a key id by the key their text
 names

[AI-generated text: this description was written autonomously by an AI
agent (Claude). Review it before relying on it or submitting it.]

The library colours a key column cell from the row's key id, so a Serato
or Rekordbox library, whose rows carry key text only, showed its keys
without colour. KeyUtils::chromaticKeyFromKeyTextAndIdFields() takes the
key id, or without one reads the text as a key, and the key colour now
uses it; with no tuning frequency those rows get the key's plain colour.

Tested on Windows: a new test checks that the key id wins over the
text, that "Am", "8A" and "1m" without an id are A minor, and that other
text is no key; it passes with the existing key and library tests.

[End of AI-generated text.]

